eld/id #uuid "2e0ff4da-3687-5c2f-a149-9fe8a300e152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528233}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e4ff63f2-f505-569f-8024-44d95016c5b9" :question/problem "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed sine function with a minimum value of $- \\frac{83}{6}$ and a maximum value of $- \\frac{22}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{- \\frac{83}{6}+(- \\frac{22}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{-83}{6}+(\\frac{-44}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{- \\frac{127}{6}}{2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{127}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=- \\frac{127}{12}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midline of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}]}
